w:st="on">Bridgeton, <st1:State w:st="on">N.J.</st1:State> On Dec. 13, 2007, Robbie 
        departed this life and went home to his eternal Father. Robbie was one 
        of three children. <br>
        <br>
        Robbie began his early school years at <st1:place w:st="on">Myron L. Powell 
        Elementary School where he was deemed gifted and talented. He completed 
        his secondary education through the Vineland School System. He was a member 
        of the <st1:place w:st="on">Shiloh Baptist Church, Port Norris. <br>
        <br>
        He leaves to cherish his memory his companion, Andrea&sup1; Jones; and 
        son, Robert &#8220;Lil Robbie&#8221; Wade Bryant Jr.; mother, Crystal 
        Joy Mosley; a brother, Matthew Bryant Jr.; a sister, Chantelle Mosley, 
        all of Millville; extended parents, Matthew and Cheryl Bryant Sr.; brother, 
        Ronald Epps; sister, Mahechea Epps, Tocarra, Ikea and Shanola Bryant, 
        all of Bridgeton; maternal grandmother, Virginia Mosley, of Cedarville; 
        paternal grandmother, Emma Wright, of Bridgeton; numerous aunts, uncles, 
        and a host of nieces, nephews, cousins and friends. <br>
        <br>
        Service will be held Saturday at noon at the <st1:place w:st="on">Shiloh 
        Baptist Church, Port Norris, with Pastor James Dunkins officiating. Interment 
        will be at the <st1:place w:st="on">Cedar Hill Memorial Park. Friends 
        may call at the church Saturday from 10 a.m. - noon. &nbsp;Written condolences 
        and tributes may be sent via to the funeral home Web site, www.edwardsandsonfuneralhome.com. 
        &nbsp;&nbsp;Services entrusted to Edwards and Son Funeral Home, Inc., 
        Bridgeton and <st1:place
w:st="on">Salem, <st1:State w:st="on">N.J.</st1:State></font></p>
